<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 40 bln levs 12-mth discount T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 40 bln levs 12-mth discount T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of 12-month discount T-bills was sold out on Monday, yielding 14.32 percent until maturity, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par of 40 billion levs and with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG3040797006</p>
<p> Maturity			  12 months</p>
<p> Par value			 40,000 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    June 30</p>
<p> Issue date			July 1</p>
<p> Maturity date		   June 30, 1998</p>
<p> Bids received		   62,900 million levs</p>
<p> Average price of bids	 86.41 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		   40,000 million levs</p>
<p> Average accepted price	87.47 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   14.32 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
